general = "AM = arithmetic mean; $\\mathbf{s}$ = sample standard deviation; $\\bar{x}$ = arithmetic mean; %CV = percent coefficient of variation; GM = geometric mean; GSD = geometric standard deviation; $s_{\\ln}$ = sample standard deviation of natural log-transformed data; $s_{\\ln}^2$ = sample variance of natural log-transformed data; %GCV = percent geometric coefficient of variation. Note: $\\pm 1 \\cdot \\text{SD}$ typically encompasses approximately $68\\%$ of data points in a normal distribution.",
